/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  hx02_condensing_steam
  =====================

  A two-stream heatExchanger whose hot side is IF97 water VAPOUR at 8 bar,
  6.4 K above its saturation temperature, against cooling water at 300 K.
  What it shows is WHERE THE OUTLET IS, not how big the duty is:

    * the duty Q comes from the eps-NTU method on SENSIBLE heat-capacity
      rates -- the vapour's c_p, with no latent term -- so it is NOT the
      duty a condenser of this area would transfer (a condensing film
      carries far more).  The unit says so in the advisory log ("a side
      changed phase").  Read Q as the sensible model's number;
    * the outlet state is then solved from H(out) = H(in) - Q/n on the
      package's own enthalpy (IF97), and the duty lands INSIDE the latent
      jump of a pure fluid: the steam leaves AT Tsat(8 bar) with a pinned
      vapour fraction, partly condensed;
    * the unit's own H_closure_gap_kW and the plant's first-law residual
      are both zero.

  Until 2026-11-13 this case did not close: the outlet search walked the
  low end of its bracket below the IF97 window, gave up, and published
  the sensible model's 300 K liquid -- a latent heat missing from the
  unit's own balance at exit 0.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

// stream state lives on disk in 0/ (per-stream files); flowsheetDict is TOPOLOGY only

units
(
    {
        name        condenserHX;
        type        heatExchanger;
        inputs      ( steam  coolingWater );
        outputs     ( wetSteam  warmWater );

        operation
        {
            area     1.0 m2;
            U        500.0 W/m2/K;
            flow     counter;
        }
    }
);
